For the purpose of this section, cruelty  means-- (a)any wilful conduct which is of such a nature as is likely to drive the woman to commit suicide or to cause grave injury or danger to life, limb or health (whether mental or physical) of the woman; or (b)harassment of the woman where such harassment is with a view to coercing her or any person related to her to meet any unlawful demand for any property or valuable Smt. Indrani Roy vs The State Of West Bengal & Anr on 8 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/87409709/
2 security or is on account of failure by her or any person related to her to meet such demand.
Ingredients of offence- The essential ingredients of the offence under sec 498A are as follows:
1) A woman was married;
2) She was subjected to cruelty;
3) Such cruelty consisted in- i) Any lawful conduct as was likely to drive such woman to commit suicide or to cause grave injury or danger to her life, limb or health whether mental or physical;
ii) harm to such woman with a view to coercing her to meet unlawful demand for property or valuable security or on account of failure of such woman or any of her relations to meet the lawful demand;
iii) the woman was subjected to such cruelty by her husband or any relation of her husband.
